<article class="env-definition" id="0F4Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F4Z">Definition <span data-tag="0F4Z">63.3.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is separated (!) and locally of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. The subsheaf $f_!\mathcal{F} \subset f_*\mathcal{F}$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0F4X" data-tag="0F4X">63.3.1</a> is called the <em>direct image with compact support</em>. </p>
